        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(anthropic): accept \"cli\" entrypoint in Claude session catalog discovery",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nClaude Code v2.x writes `entrypoint: \"cli\"` in its JSONL session files. OpenClaw's `discoverCliRecords` function in `extensions/anthropic/session-catalog.ts` only recognized `entrypoint: \"sdk-cli\"` as a valid Claude Code session entrypoint. Any session with `entrypoint: \"cli\"` was treated as an unrecognized entrypoint and silently skipped without being recorded in the catalog.\r\n\r\n**Result:** The \"CLAUDE CODE\" panel in the Control UI showed zero sessions even when multiple Claude Code projects with valid JSONL session files existed under `~/.claude/projects/`.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\n1. Updated three conditions in `discoverCliRecords` to accept `\"cli\"` alongside `\"sdk-cli\"` (TypeScript)\r\n2. Extracted `CLI_ENTRYPOINTS` set and `isCliEntrypoint()` type guard to centralize the accepted entrypoint check — adding future entrypoint values only needs a single change (TypeScript)\r\n3. Applied identical changes to the **macOS paired-node** native catalog (`MacNodeClaudeSessionCatalog.swift`) — same three conditions, same `Set<String>` + helper pattern\r\n4. Added `entrypoint: \"cli\"` regression coverage in both TypeScript and Swift test suites\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nUsers running Claude Code v2.x can now browse, search, and continue their Claude Code sessions directly from the OpenClaw Control UI session catalog, on both gateway/local and macOS paired-node paths.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n- **Root cause confirmed:** Inspected the JSONL files, found `\"entrypoint\":\"cli\"` (not `\"sdk-cli\"`); traced the skip to the entrypoint guard\r\n- **Tests (TypeScript):** `pnpm test:extension anthropic` — 17 test files, 219 tests, all passing\r\n- **Tests (Swift):** The macOS test changes mirror the same `entrypoint: \"cli\"` fixture pattern. I do not have a macOS machine to compile and run the Swift test suite locally, but the changes are structurally identical to the verified TypeScript side (same three conditions, same helper pattern, same test fixture structure)\r\n- **New regression coverage:** Added `entrypoint: \"cli\"` fixture to the sidechain/rejection test, verifying discovery, transcript reading, and correct sorting alongside `sdk-cli` on both platforms\r\n- **Screenshots (before/after):**  \r\n**Before**\r\n<img width=\"612\" height=\"1013\" alt=\"屏幕截图 2026-07-12 171314\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/377a6c6d-dd5e-4f48-87cc-fcd974755e30\" />\r\n\r\n**After**\r\n<img width=\"549\" height=\"1026\" alt=\"屏幕截图 2026-07-12 171012\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b69402b2-e06c-4a92-ac49-e2a379ce0755\" />\r\n\r\n- **Manual validation:** Gateway restarted successfully, `sessions.catalog.list` RPC returns session records for both `sdk-cli` and `cli` entrypoint sessions\r\n\r\n> This PR was authored with AI assistance (Claude Code).\r\n> - [x] I have reviewed and understand the code changes in this PR\r\n> Closes #105164",
        "branch": "fix/claude-code-cli-entrypoint-session-catalog",
